# FIRE / SMOKE DURING CONTINUED TKOF, take-off that cannot be aborted (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist booklet, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05, page 17 (owner decisions 2026-10-23, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28: the booklet is binding): the heading, every item, action, comment line and the boxed reference as printed; the booklet has no WARNING block here. The row marks are the numbers 1 to 6 as the booklet counts them. ECS shut-off PULL is the state pulled of the ECS shut-off; Fuel valve OFF is the state off of the FUEL selector; the Emergency front windows row is graded on the emergency window and the Doors row on the door release lever, both optional because this simulation has no landing and the aircraft never stands still. The printed comment lines (climb and land, the emergency landing with its reference, Evacuate) have no panel action. All other text is own wording. The fire constants, the outcome threshold and hold time, the onset window and the forbidden items are copied from ENGINE FIRE in flight and are instructor-review values; the aircraft is airborne over the runway, so the speed holds at 70 knots and the runway keeps moving.
format: 1
id: takeoff-fire-no-abort
title: T/O FIRE NO ABORT
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: "Page 17, FIRE / SMOKE DURING CONTINUED TKOF"
  verified: "2026-10-28"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: takeoff_roll
briefing:
  situation: "You have just lifted off and are climbing out low over the runway at about 70 knots with flaps in take-off position. Smoke and flames come from the engine compartment. No message is shown on the primary flight display. There is no runway left to stop on."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p100
    lv.flaps: to
    lv.gear: down
  quantities:
    fire_intensity: 40
    ground_speed_kt: 70
    airspeed_kt: 70
parameters:
  engine_fire: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: FIRE / SMOKE DURING CONTINUED TKOF
procedure[10]:
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ecs
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ecs_pulled
        severity: critical
        number: 1
        text: ECS shut-off
        action: PULL
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.ecs_shutoff
          is: pulled
  - kind: comment
    text: "If possible climb to safe height and land ASAP"
  - kind: comment
    text: "When landing assured:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_shutdown
    ordered: false
    steps[3]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 2
        text: Engine master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: 3
        text: Fuel valve
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 4
        text: Electric master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: 5
        text: Emergency front windows
        action: OPEN as necessary
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: "Carry out:"
  - kind: comment
    text: "EMERGENCY LANDING (ENGINE OFF)"
    boxed: true
    action: "(page 9)"
  - kind: comment
    text: "After standstill and when engine stopped:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_doors
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: doors_open
        severity: optional
        number: 6
        text: Doors
        action: OPEN
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: "Evacuate"
# The emergency fuel pump would feed the fire and fails the run. It is an instructor-review item.
forbidden[1]:
  - id: emerg_fuel_pump_on
    text: Switch on the emergency fuel pump
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.emerg_fuel_pump
      is: "on"
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the fire stays at a high intensity; the intensity and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: fire_spreads
    text: Fire spreads beyond the engine compartment
    hold_s: 20
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: fire_intensity
      op: gte
      value: 85
# The fire of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the aircraft flies at 70 knots from the start (the PFD airspeed starts at the same speed). The window is an instructor-review value.
# The fire shows by its flames and smoke over the cowl, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that they show within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  quantities:
    ground_speed_kt: 70
    airspeed_kt: 70
  cues[1]: flames
